# The bedside monitor (480 x 320, navigation bar at the bottom: Monitor 0-89, Alarms 89-178,
# Trends 178-267, Setup 267-356, Silence 356-480). The simulated patient desaturates 3 s
# after start and recovers at about 40 s.
#
# Watch the alarms rise: RR HIGH (medium, yellow) then SpO2 LOW (high, red, flashing).
wait 11000
shot monitor_alarm
# Silence: audio paused for 2 min, the ring counts down.
tap 418 302
wait 900
# The active alarms and their history.
tap 125 302
wait 1500
shot alarms
# Trends: 1 h, then 12 h (the desaturations of the night show at full depth).
tap 215 302
wait 1200
tap 445 49
wait 1300
shot trends
# Setup: switch to the Day display mode, back to the monitor.
tap 308 302
wait 800
tap 322 167
wait 700
tap 40 302
wait 1800
shot monitor_day
# (The README GIF ends here.)
# The table view of the trends.
tap 215 302
wait 400
tap 294 49
wait 800
shot trends_table
# Setup: lower the SpO2 low limit to 88, back to Dark, edit the patient on the keyboard.
tap 308 302
wait 400
tap 93 117
wait 200
tap 93 117
wait 400
tap 372 167
wait 600
shot setup
tap 440 74
wait 600
tap 228 85
wait 200
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
text "DOE, Jane"
wait 400
shot keyboard
tap 430 39
wait 600
# Measure the blood pressure now: the cuff inflates and deflates, then the new reading.
tap 40 302
wait 300
tap 160 255
wait 4000
shot nibp_measuring
# Recovery: SpO2 back above 90 %, the alarms clear, the history keeps them.
wait 28000
shot recovered
tap 125 302
wait 600
shot alarms_after
